      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "King Zedekiah of Judah sent Pashhur son of Malchiah and the priest Zephaniah son of Maaseiah to me with this request: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2KI.25.1+2KI.25.2+2KI.25.3+2KI.25.4+2KI.25.5+2KI.25.6+2KI.25.7+2KI.25.8+2KI.25.9+2KI.25.10+2KI.25.11"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Kgs 25.1–11",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2CH.36.17+2CH.36.18+2CH.36.19+2CH.36.20+2CH.36.21"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Chr 36.17–21",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Please speak to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " for us, because King Nebuchadnezzar of Babylonia and his army are besieging the city. Maybe the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " will perform one of his miracles for us and force Nebuchadnezzar to retreat.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.2"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " spoke to me, and I told the men who had been sent to me ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "to tell Zedekiah that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", the God of Israel, had said, “Zedekiah, I am going to defeat your army that is fighting against the king of Babylonia and his army. I will pile up your soldiers' weapons in the centre of the city. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I will fight against you with all my might, my anger, my wrath, and my fury. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I will kill everyone living in this city; people and animals alike will die of a terrible disease. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But as for you, your officials, and the people who survive the war, the famine, and the disease — I will let all of you be captured by King Nebuchadnezzar and by your enemies, who want to kill you. Nebuchadnezzar will put you to death. He will not spare any of you or show mercy or pity to any of you. I, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", have spoken.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.7"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " told me to say to the people, “Listen! I, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", am giving you a choice between the way that leads to life and the way that leads to death. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anyone who stays in the city will be killed in war or by starvation or disease. But those who go out and surrender to the Babylonians, who are now attacking the city, will not be killed; they will at least escape with their lives. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I have made up my mind not to spare this city, but to destroy it. It will be given over to the king of Babylonia and he will burn it to the ground. I, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", have spoken.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.10"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.11+JER.21.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.11",
              "JER.21.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " told me to give this message to the royal house of Judah, the descendants of David: “Listen to what I, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.11+JER.21.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.11",
              "JER.21.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", am saying. See that justice is done every day. Protect the person who is being cheated from the one who is cheating him. If you don't, the evil you are doing will make my anger burn like a fire that cannot be put out. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.11+JER.21.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.11",
              "JER.21.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You, Jerusalem, are sitting",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21.13",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "You, Jerusalem, are sitting",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; or",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "You are enthroned.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " high above the valleys, like a rock rising above the plain. But I will fight against you. You say that no one can attack you or break through your defences. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 21:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But I will punish you for what you have done. I will set your palace on fire, and the fire will burn down everything round it. I, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", have spoken.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.21.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.21.14"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
